/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  PC-SAFT WITH ASSOCIATION (Wertheim TPT1; Gross & Sadowski, Ind. Eng.
  Chem. Res. 41 (2002) 5510) -- the hydrogen-bonded liquids the
  non-associating core cannot represent, as PURE liquids at 298.15 K, 1 bar.

  The association parameters live on the component records (2B water,
  2B ethanol -- both G&S 2002 Table 1, fitted WITH the association term;
  the paper lists water with TWO sites, and the scheme is PART of the
  fit: this same set mis-curated as 4C passed the pure-density check by
  coincidence and collapsed the ethanol/water mixture flash);
  the case only declares `model PCSAFT;`, and the engine announces the
  roster it found on the records:

      [pcsaft] associating: water (2B), ethanol (2B); cross: Wolbach-Sandler

  Liquid densities PREDICTED here (goldened), vs the CRC Handbook 25 degC
  values -- each deviation stated against what the SET is fitted for:

      water    v_molar_liq -> rho_liq = 921.9 kg/m3   vs 997.05  (-7.5 % --
               the PUBLISHED trade-off of the 2-site water fit, which is
               Psat-accurate instead: -0.2 % at 358 K, +4 % at 298 K)
      ethanol  v_molar_liq -> rho_liq = 779.8 kg/m3   vs 789.3   (-1.2 %)

  What the student sees at verbosity 3 (the widened validation, ratified
  2026-08-02): the construction-time verify() now ALSO echoes, per
  associating component as a pure fluid, the converged site fractions
  X^D / X^A, the a_assoc share, and the CLOSED-FORM-vs-ITERATIVE oracle
  deviation (for nD = nA the mass-action closure collapses to a quadratic;
  the damped fixed point must land on its root -- observed machine zero).
  X^A(water) ~ 0.039: 96 % of water's sites are hydrogen-bonded at
  ambient conditions -- the physics the term adds.

  The two ops publish the standard vapour-root family (Z, v_molar) plus
  the labelled liquid root (v_molar_liq); at 1 bar both fluids carry a
  metastable vapour root beside the stable liquid.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name        water_liquid_298K;
        type        propertyPoint;
        state       { T 298.15 K;  P 1 bar;  composition { water 1.0; } }
        properties  ( Z  molarVolume );
    }
    {
        name        ethanol_liquid_298K;
        type        propertyPoint;
        state       { T 298.15 K;  P 1 bar;  composition { ethanol 1.0; } }
        properties  ( Z  molarVolume );
    }
);
